<DocsLayout title="AppDelegate Setup" section="examples">
  <h1>AppDelegate Setup</h1>
  <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground mt-1 mb-8">A complete AppDelegate wiring all four ForgePush libraries — permission, token, silent push routing, and visible push routing.</p>

  <h2>Handlers</h2>
  <p>Define your silent and visible push handlers. Keep each handler focused on a single notification type.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={handlersCode} title="PushHandlers.swift" />

  <h2>AppDelegate</h2>
  <p>Create the managers and routers as properties, add handlers at launch, and forward the standard delegate callbacks.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={appDelegateCode} title="AppDelegate.swift" />

  <h2>Token Observation</h2>
  <p>Start observing the token stream early — for example, from a service or view model — so you upload the token even if it rotates later. The stream emits <code>String?</code>, so handle the <code>nil</code> case if needed.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={tokenObserverCode} />

  <p class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-4 text-sm">
    <strong>Don't forget:</strong> Enable the <strong>Remote notifications</strong> background mode in your target's <em>Signing &amp; Capabilities</em> tab (under Background Modes) for silent pushes to wake the app.
  </p>

